<p dir=3D"auto" data-sourcepos=3D"189:1-189:125">An ElastiCache=E2=80=AFclu=
ster=E2=80=AFis a logical grouping of one or more=E2=80=AFElastiCache nodes=
. Data is partitioned across EC2 machines.</p>
<h3 dir=3D"auto" data-sourcepos=3D"191:1-191:30">
<a id=3D"user-content-use-cases--considerations-2" class=3D"anchor" aria-hi=
dden=3D"true" href=3D"https://git.epam.com/epmc-acm-public/aws-associate-tr=
aining/-/blob/master/materials/database_services/README.md#use-cases--consi=
derations-2"></a>Use cases / Considerations</h3>
<ul dir=3D"auto" data-sourcepos=3D"192:1-197:0">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"192:1-192:246">
<strong data-sourcepos=3D"192:3-192:39">Building low-latency data stores.</=
strong> Amazon ElastiCache stores non-durable datasets in the memory and fu=
rther supports real-time applications with microsecond latency and thus, he=
lps in building low-latency data stores which help many clients.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"193:1-193:295">
<strong data-sourcepos=3D"193:3-193:34">Eases backend database load.</stron=
g> Amazon ElastiCache provides caching of users' data which further reduces=
 the pressure on the user's backend database and further enables the higher=
 application scalability. This helps in reducing the operational burden and=
 thus eases the backend database load.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"194:1-194:268">
<strong data-sourcepos=3D"194:3-194:49">Accelerated performance of the appl=
ication.</strong> Amazon ElastiCache accesses the data with a microsecond l=
atency and with high throughput which further results in lightning-fast app=
lication performance. Thus it provides the accelerated performance of the a=
pplication.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"195:1-195:262">
<strong data-sourcepos=3D"195:3-195:14">Caching.</strong> Amazon ElastiCach=
e provides caching which accelerates the application and the database perfo=
rmance or further as a primary data store for use cases that don't require =
durability like the session stores, streaming gaming leaderboards and analy=
tics.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"196:1-197:0">
<strong data-sourcepos=3D"196:3-196:27">In-memory data store.</strong> Amaz=
on Elasticahe provides an in-memory key-value store(or Datastore) which fur=
ther provides ultrafast and inexpensive access to the copies of data. Furth=
er, most data stores have areas of data that are frequently accessed but ar=
e seldom updated. So, querying a database is always slower and more expensi=
ve than locating a key in the key-value pair cache.</li>
</ul>
